+# Full study
+
+Erdős Problem 1057 concerns the growth of the counting function for
+Carmichael numbers.  The selected variant records the classical upper bound
+
+`C(x) < x exp(-c (log x log log log x)/(log log x))`
+
+for some positive constant and all sufficiently large real `x`.  The exact
+Lean syntax, namespace, declaration, source interval, and provider revision
+are frozen in the intake and crosswalk records.
+
+This package separates mathematical content from provenance.  The source
+statement is a statement-provider record and carries no proof authority.  The
+claim-owned proof and audit surfaces are placeholder-free standalone Lean
+files; the canonical Master is responsible for checking their elaborated
+meaning against the frozen source expression, including every dependency
+outside the foundation profile.
+
+The lower-level DAG has one source-binding node, one analytic envelope node,
+one eventual-bound node, one existential-witness node, and one composition
+root.  No hypotheses or inference steps are removed by the distilled readable
+presentation.  Mutation and cold-replay evidence is summarized by the release
+certificate.
